From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:07:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Support both Baidu authentication schemes automatically

The Baidu LLM translation API accepts two kinds of credentials: an
API key (created on the console's 'API Key' page, sent as a Bearer
token - the scheme the API recommends) and the classic secret (from
the developer information page, used to sign requests). The engine
only implemented the sign scheme, so a key field holding an API key
produced nothing but '54001 invalid sign' replies - the error code
that covers both wrong signatures and wrong tokens.

Requests now try the Bearer scheme first and fall back to signing
on an authentication failure, remembering the working scheme per
App ID for the rest of the process. The key-field hint mentions
both accepted credentials, and the sign-scheme failure message
explains where each of them comes from.
---
