+     * Sends one request to the Baidu LLM translation API and returns the
+     * translated {@code dst} values, one per input line. The API accepts
+     * two authentication schemes, and which one works depends on what
+     * the user stored in the key field: an API key (console "API Key"
+     * page) authenticates as a Bearer token with a JSON body, while the
+     * classic secret (developer information page) signs the request as
+     * {@code MD5(appid + q + salt + secret)}. Bearer is tried first
+     * (the scheme the API recommends); an authentication failure falls
+     * back to the sign scheme, and whichever worked is remembered per
+     * App ID for the rest of the process. A reply with a single
+     * multi-line entry is split back apart. Rate limit and busy replies
+     * (54003, 59004, 54005) are retried after a pause; configuration
+     * errors fail fast.
